-- title:
--   Regularity of W[[u,v]]/(uv-π)
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative Noetherian local integral domain and let $\pi \in W$ be such that the maximal ideal of $W$ equals the principal ideal $(\pi)$, with $\pi \neq 0$; thus $W$ is a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $\pi$ (or, degenerately, a field would be excluded by $\pi \neq 0$ together with $\mathfrak m_W = (\pi)$ forcing $\pi$ to be a nonzero non-unit). Write $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\ W\ \pi$ for the quotient of the ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ of formal power series in two variables $X_0, X_1$ over $W$ by the ideal generated by the single element $X_0 X_1 - \pi$, i.e. for $W[[u,v]]/(uv - \pi)$. The assertion is that this quotient ring is a regular local ring in the sense of Mathlib's `IsRegularLocalRing`: it is a Noetherian local ring whose maximal ideal admits a generating set of cardinality equal to its Krull dimension.
--
--   This is the abstract local form of the regularity of the modular curve model at a supersingular crossing point, where two branches of the special fibre meet, as in the Deligne–Rapoport and Katz–Mazur treatments. It is used in the project's analysis of the crossing ring, for instance in the results describing elements and uniformisers of $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$ up to units and powers of the images of the variables.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_isRegularLocalRing.lean

